+## Standalone control core
+
+`HOSTGPU_NATIVE_CONTROL` builds `host_gpu_control_core` without `BUILD_ISA`,
+`USE_X86_ISA`, a simulated CPU, a `Process`, or a gem5 `System`. It reuses the
+fixed-width host protocol and the existing memory, queue, and signal state
+machines. The executable is a control-plane/self-test boundary, not a GPU
+kernel runner.
+
+From the repository root:
+
+```text
+scripts/build_gem5_mold24.sh \
+  build/HOSTGPU_NATIVE_CONTROL/dev/amdgpu/host_gpu_control_core.opt
+python3 projects/gem5/util/host_native/check_control_core.py \
+  projects/gem5/build/HOSTGPU_NATIVE_CONTROL/dev/amdgpu/host_gpu_control_core.opt
+```
+
+The audit checks the ELF type, dynamic libraries, undefined symbols, and the
+JSON self-test. `strace` is reported as unavailable when it is not installed;
+the control core itself performs no device or driver opens. Kernel execution,
+Triton integration, and the GPU compute pipeline remain later gates.
diff --git a/util/host_native/check_control_core.py b/util/host_native/check_control_core.py
